This directory contains a barebones makefile project that can be used to generate a working harness for an .exe file.

First, find the offset in bytes from the entry point of the binary to the main function of the target binary. 
This is the MAIN_OFFSET value in dllmain.cpp, which will be added to getModuleEntry() at runtime to find the address the target function was loaded to.

Then, compile:
nmake TARGET_NAME=binary_name MAIN_OFFSET=0xdeadbeef

The resulting .dll can be used as a fuzzing harness for your binary.